","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for elements like beam, stem, and accidental, where the absence of an element is ambiguous if you do not know"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"if the encoding supports that element. For Version 2.0, the supports element is expanded to allow programs to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indicate support for particular attributes or particular values. This lets applications communicate, for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example, that all system and\/or page breaks are contained in the MusicXML file."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsupports","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSupports"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLSupports","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSupports"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSupports","role":"symbol"}}}